WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.240
Dark Souls. Where do I start?

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:03.660
For the better part of a year,

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:06.520
A huge part of my life has revolved around this game.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.480
If I could sum up how i feel about it in one video,

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.740
then I wouldn't have seventy other videos dedicated to it.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:16.260
And if there's any one true testament to what this game means,

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.880
then you should just look at the content and the community

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.400
that has evolved around it.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.920
But essentially, Dark Souls, to me,

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.600
is what a video game should strive to be.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:29.360
Because games have the potential to be something that nothing else can.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.280
Not only can they put in control of a character or a world,

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.380
but they can give you an experience.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:39.600
They can use gameplay and interactivity to make you experience the world.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.600
Good games realize that you aren't just a viewer,

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:43.760
you are a player.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.000
And carefully - very carefully,

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.340
true games can be designed so that the player doesn't just witness the world around them,

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:51.800
they experience it.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:53.480
A book can't do this.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.020
A movie can't do this.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.960
Sure, these mediums can make you empathize.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.300
But they can't make you experience.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.980
Only a game can do that.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:06.800
I want this game to be the one that reminds us what some games can be.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.420
So I'm going to spend these next few minutes reflecting on what Dark Souls is.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.260
Think about Dark Souls.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:14.440
Really think about it.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.020
Do you remember your first play-through?

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:19.560
You're dropped into this world with no idea of what's going on.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.720
So you do what feels natural, you know?

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:22.580
You progress,

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:23.360
you struggle,

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:24.180
you fail,

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.980
you struggle again, and you succeed.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:29.660
One day you struggle for so long that you might even give up completely.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:31.640
And you leave this game behind.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:35.800
Now think about what I said in relation to the story of Dark Souls.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:40.340
You're an undead. You can never die, but every death brings you closer to hollowing.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:44.360
Your mind is fading and you're in this cell with no idea what's going on.

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:47.480
So you take the only option open to you.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:50.600
You progress, you struggle against the world, you fail,

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.600
you struggle again, and you succeed.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.760
One day you struggle for so long that you give up completely.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:59.840
Because undead can never die but every death brings you closer to hollowing.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.020
And once you've hollowed completely, you lose all hope.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:06.020
So the reason I said a similar thing twice

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:09.160
is because the gameplay just mirrored an experience.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:12.200
This is the story of an undead who gives up hope,

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.720
and it's the experience of a player who fights against Dark Souls.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:20.320
This is a game that has depth because it focuses on the experience.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:23.120
And Dark Souls is known as a difficult game.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:27.020
It's the story of an undead human in a world where everything is out to kill him.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:31.580
A world where dying as this undead is a traumatizing experience,

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:33.660
that you have to try and push through.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:38.740
Just like dying as a player is an irritating experience that you have to overcome.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:40.400
So it makes sense, you know?

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.220
That you should have trouble progressing in this game sometimes.

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:49.240
What a lot of people don't understand is that Dark Souls isn't difficult for the sake of being difficult.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:52.760
Its difficulty comes as a result of a deeper design philosophy,

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:57.280
From Software have actively designed their game around something that only games have:

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:58.340
A failure state.

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:02.140
Death in video games is something we take for granted at this point.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:07.760
But in Dark Souls, death and failure are designed to give you that feeling of struggle and triumph.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:12.080
It's also used to immerse yourself in a world where death doesn't end your life,

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:15.300
but it brings you closer and closer to giving up.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:18.060
People often say, 'it's too difficult,'

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:20.220
or, 'it doesn't explain things to you,'

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:23.580
these are insults leveled at the Souls series regularly, and...

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:24.260
They're right.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.880
Dark Souls is too difficult for some people.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:30.200
Dark Souls also doesn't go out of its way to explain things to you.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:33.180
But here's something you have to understand about Dark Souls,

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:36.580
it's a game that doesn't dumb down the experience for the benefit

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:38.600
of the so-called 'mass-market appeal.'

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:42.700
It does its own thing, regardless of whether some people will be turned off, and

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:47.180
in doing so it's become something infinitely more valuable and pure.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:51.280
From's philosophy revolves around making this good game first,

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:53.700
and trusting that people will come, and

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.880
this has happened, slowly, you know?

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:58.120
Demon's Souls came out, and it was a niche hit,

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.740
Dark Souls came out, and

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:03.560
even two years after the game came out, people are still picking it up

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:04.820
due to word of mouth.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:09.040
As a result, the Souls series doesn't need huge marketing efforts behind it,

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:15.440
because it's become this industry icon through word of mouth and people telling each other they should play it.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:18.780
You know, someone said something really great to me, recently.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:24.920
He said, 'You know, From Software, they aren't afraid to put things in their game that people will miss.'

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:28.680
And, that's such a perfectly beautiful statement.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:32.940
If I had to choose any statement that represented Dark Souls, I'd probably choose this one.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:35.260
It's the reason the game has so much depth,

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:39.980
because they don't compromise on game design, just so every player can see an area,

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:44.200
or so that every player can understand and play their game as soon as they start.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:48.520
When I say that you might not see certain things, I'm not just talking about how

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:53.780
the DLC is located in a hard-to-see cave near an optional boss that can only be accessed

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:55.860
if you kill certain enemies in the right order.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:59.840
No, I'm also talking about how they don't shove the story down your throat,

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:03.620
or how the game locks you out of certain areas if you're not good enough to beat them.

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:05.280
Let me explain that better.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:07.000
Imagine if you were reading a book.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:10.560
You're reading a book and then all of a sudden the book shuts itself and says 'Stop!'

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.020
'You're not good enough to read me!'

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:14.940
'I'm going to lock away parts, so you have to earn them.'

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:18.200
Dark Souls sets itself apart from other game in this way.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:22.980
And this is just one of the reasons it's come to be considered a 'pure' gaming experience.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:27.040
It's something, I think, that could help games  remember what they can be.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:32.280
I think games should, generally, focus on what makes them different from other forms of media.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:36.720
And that's something that From Software has captured in... A lot of different ways.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:41.180
But Dark Souls doesn't just lock you out of content by being difficult.

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:45.380
In fact, I think one of the biggest reasons Dark Souls is considered difficult

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:49.320
is not because it's 'hard,' but because it's hard to get into.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:54.120
And while I see this as a bit of a problem, since they plan to fix this in Dark Souls II,

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.600
and make the game more accessible,

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:59.660
some fans will even argue that the inaccessibility of Dark Souls is a plus,

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:04.500
because it makes those first few hours of torment and struggle even more rewarding

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:06.400
when you finally learn how to play.

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:10.700
But it's not just the gameplay in Dark Souls that's cryptic.

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:13.180
And anyone who's on my channel knows this.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:17.880
Dark Souls also approached the concept of story in a game in a unique way.

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:21.700
The story elements are cryptic and hidden down to the last little detail.

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:25.180
And while you might have some idea of what happened by the end of the game...

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:27.340
Most players actually just end up thinking,

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:28.840
'Why the fuck am I on fire?'

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:35.040
There's actually a beautiful little story behind why the souls games were created with these cryptic, hidden stories.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:37.020
I'm sure many of you have realized this, but

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:41.020
Dark Souls is a western-style RPG created in Japan.

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:46.500
And that's a bit strange. It even has English voice-actors to convey this feeling more accurately.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.240
So, why is this? Why is this a vision?

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:52.420
Well, when Miyazaki, the game's director, was a child,

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:54.620
he loved reading western fantasy.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:58.020
He loved the stories, the settings, and he was inspired.

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:02.460
And so Dark Souls was created in this western RPG format.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:04.380
But, there's more to this story.

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:06.740
Miyazaki couldn't read English very well,

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:10.520
so when he read these western fantasy novels, he had gaps.

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:13.280
And you might be able to see where I'm going with this.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:16.340
Some parts of these books, he just couldn't read.

00:07:16.340 --> 00:07:20.840
And so while he had this vision of decaying castles and brave knights,

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:24.000
he had to use his imagination to fill the gaps.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.360
And in doing so, he created a story that was partly his own.

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:29.940
And a story that was richer because of this fact.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:31.320
Sound familiar?

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:34.580
When we play Dark Souls, we create our own stories.

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.100
Just like Miyazaki did.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.940
We read item descriptions, we listen to dialogue

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:44.680
and from the bones and fragments of a story, we slowly, carefully craft this vision of a world.

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:48.860
Some people, like me, bring this vision to life through videos.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:50.780
We call this vision, 'lore.'

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:56.600
Some of us share our lore with others, and discover other people's stories on image boards and forums,

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:58.960
inspiring and challenging great ideas.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:03.560
And this is what has kept this incredible community alive way longer than you'd expect.

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:08.640
By creating a game that intentionally leaves things for you to discover and speculate on,

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:11.540
we now have one of the strongest communities on YouTube.

00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:15.240
And we exist across hundreds of pages of forums and wikis.

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:20.100
There's a reason people were still coming into this game years after the initial marketing push.

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:24.180
It's because, we in the Dark Souls community talk about this game.

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:28.440
We share our experience and there are thousands of people who play,

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.980
just because they get that comment from a friend that says,

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:33.140
'Dude, you have to play this game,' or

00:08:33.140 --> 00:08:34.160
when someone says,

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:35.540
'You haven't played Dark Souls?'

00:08:35.540 --> 00:08:40.240
I can't imagine not having a friend to talk to about my experiences in this game, you know?

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:43.900
The thrill you get when your world is invaded by another player, or

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:48.080
the venting of frustration that you have to do when you've been stuck on a boss for four hours.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:52.540
And then the eventual ecstasy you get when you overcome and obstacle that was in your way,

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:56.420
it's just one of those games that was destined to find a home on the internet.

00:08:56.420 --> 00:09:00.400
Full of people who need to share and tell others about this experience.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:03.680
And in this way, the game actually kind of sells itself.

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:08.720
I recently got invited to the Namco-Bandai offices in San Jose in the states,

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:13.560
and I managed to meet al these people who were behind the marketing of Dark Souls and Dark Souls II.

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:17.020
And, the thing is, they realized that this game is different.

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:21.180
They realize it has this effect on people where word of mouth will sell their game.

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:24.720
And really, they just have to allow From Software to fulfill their vision.

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:28.300
And I can't think of any better publisher to publish this actually.

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:33.020
I met with Bryan Hong who's the director of marketing for Dark Souls and Dark Souls II,

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:37.640
and he put it so well. They don't have to change Dark Souls to suit the market.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:41.240
Just like Apple didn't create a PC to suit the market,

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:45.600
the market eventually realized their vision and came around to them.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:48.440
And that's what I think is happening with Dark Souls.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:51.900
And I think that this is a game that will come to define a generation.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:54.960
And I'm actually honored to be a part of it with you guys.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:10:00.160
Soon, you'll be able to click here and kindle the bonfire so that we can make this channel better together.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:05.540
In the comments of this video, I'd love for you to tell me your favorite little piece of gameplay design in Dark Souls.

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:09.700
I could have made this video much longer if I talked about all my favorite mechanics and bits,

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:11.960
but I decided to keep it short, but sweet.

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:16.320
For example though, I could quote so many beautiful pieces of gameplay design

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:17.760
from the design-works book.

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:22.100
And these have interviews with the director and developer, so

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:25.220
I think I might just read one of my favorite quotes right now,

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:30.420
so one of them is about his design of the undead, uhh, the undead dragon.

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:31.840
And, he says,

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:33.580
and Miyazaki says,

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:37.420
"Most people don't believe me when I say this, but a certain kind of refinement,

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:38.320
"elegance, and

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.500
"dignity are very important to me.

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:46.080
"I usually tell the designers that flat out grotesque or splatter-type design will not get past me.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:52.360
"This has everything to do with my own personal sensibilities and it's something that I apply to every design that I approve.

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:57.080
"It's a little hard to describe if you were to ask me... Well, what do you mean by dignity?

00:10:57.080 --> 00:11:00.640
"I guess the best answer I can provide you is right here, in this book.

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:04.280
"In every design in Dark Souls you see within these pages,

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:08.480
"My idea of dignity is something I pursue with every project I work on."

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:12.180
And then one of the other designers tells a story, he says,

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:14.900
"I remember when I was drawing the undead dragon.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:20.720
"I submitted a design draft that depicted a dragon swarming with maggots, and other gross things.

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:27.700
"Miyazaki handed this back to me, saying, 'this isn't dignified. Don't rely on the gross fact to portray and undead dragon.'

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:35.560
"'Can't you instead try to convey the deep sorrow of a magnificent beast, doomed to a slow and possibly endless descent into ruin?'"

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:39.780
And, like, just look at how they succeeded with this in terms of design.

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:41.620
This is an undead dragon.

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:46.800
Doomed to live the rest of its life clinging to cliffs while its brethren fly through the skies,

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:49.020
and instead it's here, rotting away.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:54.200
If you aggravate it, it tries to breath fire, but vomits out bile and poison instead.

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:59.080
I challenge you guys to look deeper into every aspect of design in this game.

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:02.900
And, for example, where some people just see a rotting dragon,

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:09.700
others will see that deep sorrow of a magnificent beast, doomed to die a slow and possibly endless descent into ruin.

00:12:10.220 --> 00:12:14.420
Anyway, I'll catch you guys next time as we dive head-first into Dark Souls II.

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:18.200
There's going to be so much content on this channel, so keep your eyes out.

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:18.860
Later.

